  name "the-object-of-a-call-places-arguments-at-the-callees-positions"
  note "A compiled call keeps each argument at the position its parameter stands at in the callee, whatever order the call writes them in: `std.collection.setting` declares its receiver, then `key`, then `value`, so the call's operations stand at those positions, with nothing at the receiver's, which the call writes in front."
